<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>sum arithmatic sequence q3</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The learners of a Junior School are building an open-air amphitheatre for drama and music festivals. The seats are arranged in rows. The numbers of seats form an arithmetic progression (AP). Row {@p@} has {@tp@} seats and row {@q@} has {@tq@} seats.</p>

<p>(a) Find the common difference, \(d\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the number of seats in row 1, which is the first term, \(a\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) The amphitheatre has {@Nr@} rows. Find the total number of seats.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Find the total number of seats from row {@s@} to row {@Nr@}.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>

<p>(e) A school event needs exactly {@target@} seats. The rows are filled in order, starting from row 1. How many rows are needed?</p>
<p>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3> Worked Solution.</h3>
<p>Row {@p@} has {@tp@} seats and row {@q@} has {@tq@} seats. The number of seats forms an arithmetic progression (AP).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common difference:</strong></p>
<p>Use the term formula \( T_n = a + (n-1)d \) for the two rows given.</p>
<p>Row {@p@}:</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@p@} } = a + ({@p@} - 1)d = {@tp@} \]</p>
<p>\[ a + {@p-1@}d = {@tp@} \qquad \text{(equation 1)} \]</p>
<p>Row {@q@}:</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@q@} } = a + ({@q@} - 1)d = {@tq@} \]</p>
<p>\[ a + {@q-1@}d = {@tq@} \qquad \text{(equation 2)} \]</p>
<p>Subtract equation 1 from equation 2. This eliminates \(a\):</p>
<p>\[ (a + {@q-1@}d) - (a + {@p-1@}d) = {@tq@} - {@tp@} \]</p>
<p>\[ {@q-p@}d = {@tq - tp@} \]</p>
<p>Divide both sides by {@q-p@}:</p>
<p>\[ d = \frac{ {@tq - tp@} }{ {@q-p@} } = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Each row has {@ta1@} more seats than the row before it.</p>
<p>(b) <strong>First term:</strong></p>
<p>Use \( T_n = a + (n-1)d \) with \( T_{ {@p@} } = {@tp@} \):</p>
<p>\[ a + ({@p@} - 1) \times {@d@} = {@tp@} \]</p>
<p>\[ a + {@(p-1)*d@} = {@tp@} \]</p>
<p>\[ a = {@tp@} - {@(p-1)*d@} = {@ta2@} \]</p>
<p>Row 1 has {@ta2@} seats.</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Total seats in {@Nr@} rows:</strong></p>
<p>Use \( a = {@a@} \), \( d = {@d@} \) and \( n = {@Nr@} \):</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@Nr@} } = \frac{ {@Nr@} }{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + ({@Nr@} - 1) \times {@d@}\right) \]</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@Nr@} } = \frac{ {@Nr@} }{2}\left({@2*a@} + {@(Nr-1)*d@}\right) = \frac{ {@Nr@} }{2} \times {@2*a + (Nr-1)*d@} = {@ta3@} \]</p>
<p>The amphitheatre has {@ta3@} seats.</p>

<p>(d) <strong>Seats from row {@s@} to row {@Nr@}:</strong></p>
<p>This total is all {@Nr@} rows without the first {@s-1@} rows. So we need \( S_{ {@s-1@} } \):</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@s-1@} } = \frac{ {@s-1@} }{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + ({@s-1@} - 1) \times {@d@}\right) = {@Ss1@} \]</p>
<p>Subtract:</p>
<p>\[ {@SN@} - {@Ss1@} = {@ta4@} \]</p>
<p>Rows {@s@} to {@Nr@} have {@ta4@} seats.</p>

<p>(e) <strong>Number of rows needed for {@target@} seats:</strong></p>
<p>Put \( S_n = {@target@} \), \( a = {@a@} \) and \( d = {@d@} \) into the formula:</p>
<p>\[ \frac{n}{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + (n-1) \times {@d@}\right) = {@target@} \]</p>
<p>Multiply both sides by 2 and simplify the bracket:</p>
<p>\[ n\left({@2*a - d@} + {@d@}n\right) = {@2*target@} \]</p>
<p>\[ {@d@}n^2 + {@2*a - d@}n - {@2*target@} = 0 \]</p>
<p>Divide every term by {@d@}:</p>
<p>\[ n^2 + {@2*c - 1@}n - {@2*target/d@} = 0 \]</p>
<p>Factorise:</p>
<p>\[ (n - {@m@})(n + {@2*c - 1 + m@}) = 0 \]</p>
<p>So \( n = {@m@} \) or \( n = {@r2@} \).</p>
<p>The number of rows cannot be negative, so \( n = {@ta5@} \). The event needs {@ta5@} rows.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
